{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"9d4a5f1f-1483-40e7-8af5-d96723468e15","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have reviewed the user request, the attached screenshot, and the corresponding AutoByteus task (`project_task_ad5f497a-6825-41f1-ab99-5c67b4a619f0`):\n\n### Issue Summary \u0026 Preliminary Finding\n- **Symptom:** When a user attaches an image context file to a message (e.g. `\"her\"`) in a Daily Assistant run using the Antigravity (AGY) runtime, the agent replies: *\"It looks like the image or text didn't come through yet! Could you paste the image here...\"*\n- **Root Cause Confirmed via Probe:** \n  - Probing the `agy` CLI streaming input with `{\"type\": \"image\", ...}` results in:\n    ```json\n    {\"event\":\"result\",\"result\":{\"status\":\"ERROR\",\"error\":\"stream input content block type \\\"image\\\" is not supported (only \\\"text\\\")\"}}\n    ```\n  - The `agy` CLI stream input only accepts `text` content blocks in user turn events.\n  - However, the `agy` agent **does** have the built-in `view_file` tool. When an attached image's file path is provided in the prompt/context text (or instructed as context files), the agent immediately invokes `view_file` on the local file path and inspects/understands the image perfectly (as demonstrated in `probeB.out`).\n\n### Repository \u0026 Workspace Context\n- Dedicated worktree is already established at `/Users/normy/autobyteus_org/autobyteus-worktrees/agy-image-context-input` on branch `codex/agy-image-context-input`.\n\nShall we bootstrap the ticket folder `tickets/in-progress/agy-image-context-input` following the software engineering workflow and begin the investigation and implementation plan?\n","duration_seconds":81.879711,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":213439,"output_tokens":2876,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":553117,"total_tokens":216315}}}
